WEBVTT

00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:01.779
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.860
In this lesson, we will make alerts reach the intended audience.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:11.149
Repeated messages create noise, while incomplete contacts and device preferences

00:00:11.149 --> 00:00:13.510
can leave intended recipients unreachable.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.989
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:16.989 --> 00:00:18.879
practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.470
An administrator creates notification rules for new calls, builds an

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:28.099
Officers distribution list and runs a communication test before going live.

00:00:28.599 --> 00:00:31.120
A dispatch only helps if it reaches people.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.679
This is where you confirm members can actually be contacted.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.680
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.899
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:41.569 --> 00:00:42.870
Notification rules.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.989
Rules that alert chosen people when calls, statuses or other events happen.

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:51.399
Create notification rules for the events officers and

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:53.040
administrators need to know about.

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:54.929
Distribution lists.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.470
Reusable recipient lists, including email lists.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.499
Create lists for groups you message often, such as Officers.

00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:04.440
Communication Tests.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.730
Test messages that show whether members can be reached.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.479
Run a communication test before going live and after major changes.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.499
Chat.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:15.290
Team chat for members.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.660
Create channels for your teams once chat is enabled.

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:20.029
Inbox.

00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:21.530
Messages sent to you.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.300
Make sure members have added a mobile number or email address

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:26.950
and installed the Responder app.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.690
Availability also depends on Messaging.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.199
Check access in the target department.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.860
Sent Messages.

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:35.509
Messages you have sent.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.250
Make sure members have added a mobile number or email address

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.000
and installed the Responder app.

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:43.779
Availability also depends on Messaging.

00:01:44.199 --> 00:01:46.289
Check access in the target department.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.829
New Message.

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:51.619
Send a message, poll or callback request to members.

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:55.180
Make sure members have added a mobile number or email address

00:01:55.239 --> 00:01:56.810
and installed the Responder app.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.560
Availability also depends on Messaging.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.980
Check access in the target department.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.010
Chatbot and Assistant integration settings.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.390
Connect the Resgrid Assistant to chat platforms and choose what it may do.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:13.090
Make sure members have added a mobile number or email address

00:02:13.149 --> 00:02:14.729
and installed the Responder app.

00:02:15.329 --> 00:02:19.910
Account linking associates a member with a configured external assistant platform.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.690
Confirm a platform is configured, generate a short-lived linking code, and

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.930
complete linking in the intended platform.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:30.489
Review the linked identity and a controlled permitted action.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.379
Keep the temporary code out of the recording.

00:02:33.869 --> 00:02:36.650
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:38.140
recording the live workflow.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.609
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:02:42.079 --> 00:02:42.730
Step 1.

00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:46.409
Confirm member contacts and notification preferences.

00:02:46.869 --> 00:02:47.510
Step 2.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:52.000
Create an Officers distribution list and a focused notification rule.

00:02:52.489 --> 00:02:53.229
Step 3.

00:02:53.649 --> 00:02:57.660
Run an explicit communication test and review the recorded outcomes.

00:02:58.319 --> 00:02:59.789
Now verify the result.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:04.189
Ask test recipients to confirm the actual channel and time received.

00:03:04.609 --> 00:03:08.009
Review missing or failed results and the intended audience.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.210
A common problem to watch for: A provider handoff is not confirmed delivery.

00:03:13.679 --> 00:03:17.870
Staffing suppression, recipient selection, and contact eligibility

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.659
each deserve a separate check.

00:03:20.309 --> 00:03:21.909
Your practice task is simple.

00:03:22.259 --> 00:03:24.329
Send only to the demo audience.

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:29.220
Record recipients, observed receipts, failures, and follow-up actions;

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.390
compare with the expected audience.

00:03:31.689 --> 00:03:35.619
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

